{"kind":"panel","id":"6e3182ab-1d9a-4f36-bf83-be6adaa74500","type":"59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c","name":"Panel","nick":"The Cliff","desc":"A panel for custom notes and text values","box":[0,-300,520,220],"src":[],"text":"The Cliff - lesson 2 of the Alpaca4d Playground.\n\nThe River's plank, C24 300 x 50 mm, built into the cliff and sticking out 4 m over the drop, with the alpaca, 0.6 kN, standing at its tip.\n\nCheck it by hand: PL^3 / 3EI = 0.6 x 4^3 / (3 x 10 500 000 x 0.3 x 0.05^3 / 12) = 390 mm, 16 times the River's 24.4 mm. The panel Z in m reads it; Model View draws it true to scale.\n\nTry: wire a toggle set to False into the Support's Ry, and see Run Analysis fail; or move the load to End Points' S.","colour":[0,0,0,0]}
